WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.072
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:09.188
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.488 --> 00:00:16.540
Unit twenty: Test Day Strategy and Review. Today you will manage time, stress and every section on test day.

4
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.458
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.505
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:25.235
Strategy.

7
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.760
Strategy means a plan to reach a goal.

8
00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:31.268
Have a strategy for each section.

9
00:00:31.883 --> 00:00:34.222
Your turn. Say: Strategy.

10
00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:38.219
Strategy.

11
00:00:38.983 --> 00:00:39.845
Timing.

12
00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.641
Timing means how you use time.

13
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.553
Practise your timing.

14
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.326
Your turn. Say: Timing.

15
00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:50.970
Timing.

16
00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:52.845
Adaptive.

17
00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.314
Adaptive means changing to match your level.

18
00:00:56.917 --> 00:00:58.359
Reading is adaptive.

19
00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.659
Your turn. Say: Adaptive.

20
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.292
Adaptive.

21
00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.039
Focus.

22
00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.119
Focus means to give full attention.

23
00:01:11.717 --> 00:01:13.600
Focus on the first questions.

24
00:01:14.217 --> 00:01:16.799
Your turn. Say: Focus.

25
00:01:19.633 --> 00:01:20.600
Focus.

26
00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:22.061
Calm.

27
00:01:23.050 --> 00:01:25.026
Calm means relaxed and not worried.

28
00:01:25.617 --> 00:01:26.583
Stay calm.

29
00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:29.464
Your turn. Say: Calm.

30
00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.115
Calm.

31
00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:35.014
Mock test.

32
00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:39.026
Mock test means a practice test like the real one.

33
00:01:39.617 --> 00:01:41.001
Take a mock test.

34
00:01:41.617 --> 00:01:44.199
Your turn. Say: Mock test.

35
00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.301
Mock test.

36
00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.283
Technical check.

37
00:01:51.283 --> 00:01:53.736
Technical check means a test of your equipment.

38
00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.361
Do a technical check first.

39
00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.962
Your turn. Say: Technical check.

40
00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.057
Technical check.

41
00:02:04.817 --> 00:02:05.644
Review.

42
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.139
Review means to look at again.

43
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.134
Review your mistakes.

44
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.484
Your turn. Say: Review.

45
00:02:16.333 --> 00:02:17.033
Review.

46
00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:21.623
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.483 --> 00:02:25.354
Visal, how should I prepare in the last week?

48
00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:37.705
Take full timed practice tests, review your mistakes and sleep well. Do not learn many new things the night before, because rest helps your performance.

49
00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:40.863
What should I remember about each section?

50
00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:52.718
In Reading and Listening be accurate from the start, because the test adapts. In Writing keep to the time limits, and in Speaking answer fully without long pauses.

51
00:02:53.817 --> 00:02:55.224
How do I stay calm?

52
00:02:56.317 --> 00:03:08.269
Check your equipment early, breathe slowly and treat each task as a separate chance. If one answer goes badly, forget it and focus on the next task.

53
00:03:09.433 --> 00:03:10.736
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.583 --> 00:03:15.975
Grammar focus: Strategy: prepare, focus, recover.

55
00:03:16.275 --> 00:03:17.496
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:21.541
I take a full mock test every week under real timing.

57
00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:25.982
If a task goes badly, I move on and focus on the next one.

58
00:03:26.933 --> 00:03:34.497
Practise under real timing, check your equipment, and stay calm. Treat each task as a new chance and do not worry about the last one.

59
00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.796
Be careful! Don't say: I study new topics all night.

60
00:03:40.733 --> 00:03:42.675
Say: I rest before the test.

61
00:03:42.975 --> 00:03:44.057
Sleep well.

62
00:03:44.867 --> 00:03:47.554
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:49.310
Test Day.

64
00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:52.526
Channary does a technical check of her headphones in the morning.

65
00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:56.450
She starts the Reading section and answers carefully.

66
00:03:57.467 --> 00:04:00.604
One Listening question is difficult, so she moves on.

67
00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:05.028
In Speaking she answers every question without long pauses.

68
00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:08.416
She finishes the test calm and satisfied.

69
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.455
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:14.317 --> 00:04:16.316
Before the test you should do a blank.

71
00:04:16.616 --> 00:04:20.769
A, party. B, long trip. C, technical check.

72
00:04:24.333 --> 00:04:26.751
The answer is C: technical check.

73
00:04:27.917 --> 00:04:30.555
Adaptive sections need blank from the start.

74
00:04:30.855 --> 00:04:34.856
A, accuracy. B, guessing. C, silence.

75
00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.365
The answer is A: accuracy.

76
00:04:41.517 --> 00:04:44.050
If a task goes badly, you should blank.

77
00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:47.888
A, complain. B, move on. C, stop.

78
00:04:51.433 --> 00:04:53.665
The answer is B: move on.

79
00:04:54.817 --> 00:04:56.956
What helps performance the night before?

80
00:04:57.256 --> 00:05:01.188
A, new topics. B, no sleep. C, rest.

81
00:05:04.733 --> 00:05:06.791
The answer is C: rest.

82
00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.683
How does Channary finish?

83
00:05:09.983 --> 00:05:13.857
A, calm and satisfied. B, worried. C, angry.

84
00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.934
The answer is A: calm and satisfied.

85
00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:24.401
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.133
What is your plan for test day?

87
00:05:35.950 --> 00:05:37.450
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:50.785
I will check my equipment early and arrive calm. In each section I will focus on the current task and manage my time. If something goes badly, I will move on and focus on the next question.

89
00:05:51.085 --> 00:05:52.922
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:53.817 --> 00:05:59.406
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: prepare, focus, recover.

91
00:05:59.706 --> 00:06:05.075
Today's value is self-discipline. Control your habits, so your habits do not control you.

92
00:06:05.375 --> 00:06:11.792
Congratulations! You have finished Online TOEFL preparation. See you in Online TOEIC preparation!

93
00:06:12.092 --> 00:06:14.640
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

